# efficientnet_lite0_waste8_u8.hef - CURRENT, the one this solution deploys.
#   4,551,414 bytes, built 2026-09-07. ImageNet mean/std are a normalization
#   layer inside the HEF, so the device feeds raw uint8 NHWC RGB and needs no
#   float preprocessing on the host. That matches what the RKNN and cvimodel
#   builds do, which is what keeps one preprocessing definition across every
#   accelerator in this solution.
#   Quantised with optimization_level=2 -- a quantisation-aware distillation
#   finetune, 8 epochs -- with bias correction kept on and calibset_size set
#   explicitly, over 2048 class-balanced uint8 training crops (calibration npy
#   sha256 045359d79cd4ed20a9e239492000df3e2d1bf222a67ec13f44ae82835ddc4967).
#   Compiling it needs a GPU visible inside the DFC container (docker run
#   --gpus all); with no GPU the DFC reduces the optimization level and says so
#   in one log line instead of failing.
#   Compile timings: parse 7s / optimize 1255s / compile 39s.
#   Measured on a Hailo-8 over the full 7417-image val set: material top-1
#   0.8889 (fp32 CPU 0.8877 on the same images), China-4 0.9507, agreement vs
#   CPU 0.9581, p50 3.166 ms / p95 3.249 ms.
#
# 4e3b9640d0e07aa5ac4235fcadedb8a06ce24568f50c57dcb4dd8bbd0f4aa89e - superseded.
#   The same graph at optimization_level=1, 4,576,932 bytes. Measured 0.8637
#   top-1 on the same 7417 images, 2.40 points below fp32. Do not deploy it.
#
# efficientnet_lite0_waste8.hef - superseded packaging of the same backbone.
#   4,519,376 bytes, built 2026-09-06. The graph carries no normalization
#   layer, so it needs ImageNet-normalised float input prepared on the host.
#   Kept for continuity with the DFC emulator comparison that produced
#   agreement 0.890 against CPU/native on 200 validation images.
#
# mobilenetv3s_waste8.hef - superseded backbone, kept as the INT8 contrast.
#   2,498,997 bytes. Compiles cleanly but the INT8 graph collapses to a single
#   class (agreement 0.115 vs CPU/native on 200 validation images). Not
#   deployable; this is the failure that caused the switch to
#   EfficientNet-Lite0.
#
# Open-vocabulary SigLIP 2 vision tower: `hailo parser` passes end to end with
# no unsupported op (HAR
# af7de30b5c3c2938381f235821b3279120daa072c11e948faf451f9bcfeee471), but
# `hailo optimize` (INT8 PTQ, 256 calibration images, optimization_level=1)
# fails at layer ne_activation_mul_and_add78 with
# NegativeSlopeExponentNonFixable: "Desired shift is 16.0, but op has only 8
# data bits". No optimized HAR, no HEF. Source:
